  "note": "Specs that must run at ONE worker. Everything else may run concurrently. Two mechanisms put a spec here. FOCUS: it opens the preferences window or drives a context menu, and throng closes menus when its window loses focus, so a second headed app closes them underneath it. CPU: it drives long-running real shells (ping, findstr loops), which starve at high worker counts and time out - the same failure mode that keeps CI at one worker per shard (ci.yml). Membership is the mechanism plus anything measured failing at 6 workers, not observed failures alone, because contention produces a different failure set every run. Guarded by packages/ui/tests/unit/shard-plan.test.ts. See docs/testing.md. TIMING: it asserts a wall-clock ceiling (SC-002's two seconds from daemon kill to notice), which contention breaks without anything having regressed - measured at 2039ms with six workers against a 2000ms budget, where 1200ms of it is the grace by design.",
